          </svg>
          <a href="/services" class="hover:text-[#A61E22] transition font-medium">Services</a>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" />
          </svg>
          <span class="text-[#A61E22] font-semibold">Lock Repair</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Schema: Breadcrumbs -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Lock Repair", "item": "https://www.1stcapitallocksmith.com/services/lock-repair/" }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: Service -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Lock Repair in Delaware",
    "description": "Professional lock repair services for residential and commercial properties throughout Delaware. 1st Capital Locksmith fixes stiff locks, broken deadbolts, jammed door locks, damaged lock cylinders, and more across Kent County.",
    "provider": {
      "@type": "LocalBusiness",
      "name": "1st Capital Locksmith",
      "telephone": "+13027350050",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "addressLocality": "Dover",
        "addressRegion": "DE",
        "addressCountry": "US"
      }
    },
    "areaServed": {
      "@type": "State",
      "name": "Delaware"
    },
    "serviceType": "Lock Repair"
  })} />

  <!-- Schema: FAQ -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does lock repair cost in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Lock repair cost depends on the type of lock, the nature of the problem, and whether any parts are needed. In many cases lock repair is significantly less expensive than full replacement. We provide a clear upfront quote before any work begins. Call (302) 735-0050 for a fast estimate."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can a stiff or hard-to-turn lock be repaired without replacing it?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "In most cases, yes. A stiff lock is usually caused by internal wear, a misaligned door, or a dried-out mechanism that needs lubrication and adjustment. Our locksmiths diagnose the root cause and repair it on-site whenever possible, saving you the cost of a full replacement."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Should I repair or replace a broken lock?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "It depends on the extent of the damage and the quality of the existing hardware. Many locks can be repaired quickly and affordably. If the lock is severely damaged, very old, or low-quality, replacement is often the smarter long-term choice. We'll give you an honest assessment and let you decide."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can you repair a lock that was damaged in a break-in attempt?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. We assess locks damaged by forced entry, attempted picking, or drilling. In many cases parts of the lock can be repaired, though a lock that has been compromised in a break-in attempt is often best replaced entirely for your security. We'll advise you honestly on the right call."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you repair commercial locks and office locks in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. We repair commercial door locks, office locks, storefront locks, mortise locks, and other commercial hardware throughout Delaware. We can work around your business hours to minimize disruption."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How quickly can you respond to a lock repair call in Delaware?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "We dispatch as quickly as possible to lock repair calls throughout Delaware. For urgent situations where a lock is failing or a door cannot be secured, call (302) 735-0050 and we'll prioritize your call."
        }
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative min-h-[340px] md:min-h-[550px] flex items-center text-white py-10 md:py-20"
    style="background-image: url('/images/lock-repair.jpg'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/72"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-6 z-10">
      <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-xs md:text-sm mb-2 md:mb-4">Lock Repair Services — Delaware</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-3 md:mb-6 max-w-3xl leading-tight">
        Professional Lock Repair in Delaware — Fix It Right, the First Time
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm md:text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-5 md:mb-8">
        Stiff key? Jammed deadbolt? Lock that won't turn or won't latch? Don't wait until it fails completely. 1st Capital Locksmith diagnoses and repairs locks for homes and businesses throughout Delaware — fast, on-site, with honest pricing before we start.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <a
          href="tel:3027350050"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-bold text-base md:text-lg hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
        >
          Call (302) 735-0050
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-white px-6 py-3 md:px-8 md:py-4 text-white font-semibold text-sm md:text-base hover:bg-white hover:text-[#1A1F22] transition"
        >
          Get a Free Quote
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trust Bar -->
  <section class="bg-[#0E1B2F] py-8">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">All Lock Types</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Deadbolts, Knobs, Levers & More</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">On-Site Repair</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">We Come Directly to Your Property</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Honest Assessment</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Repair vs. Replace — Straight Talk</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#A61E22]">Upfront Pricing</p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mt-1">Clear Quote Before We Start</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="bg-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Delaware's Lock Repair Experts</p>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6 leading-snug">
            Lock Repair Service for Homes & Businesses Throughout Delaware
          </h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A lock that's misbehaving is more than just a minor inconvenience — it's a security liability. Whether your key is getting progressively harder to turn, your deadbolt doesn't fully extend, your lock feels loose in the door, or a break-in attempt has left your hardware compromised, a struggling lock needs professional attention before it fails entirely.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            1st Capital Locksmith provides professional lock repair services for residential and commercial properties throughout Delaware. Our locksmiths carry the tools and parts to diagnose and repair most lock problems on-site in a single visit. We take the time to properly assess what's causing the issue so we can fix the root problem — not just the symptom.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            We repair deadbolts, knob locks, lever handle locks, mortise locks, padlocks, sliding door locks, and more across Dover, Milford, Smyrna, Camden, Harrington, and all of Kent County, Delaware. When repair isn't the right answer, we'll tell you that too — and handle the replacement on the same visit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Photo Slot 1 -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-[#F8F8F5] aspect-[4/3] flex items-center justify-center">
            <img
              src="/images/lock-repair-service.jpg"
              alt="Professional lock repair service on a residential door in Delaware"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
              width="600"
              height="450"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="bg-[#F8F8F5] rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-6">Lock Problems We Repair:</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              {[
                "Stiff or Hard-to-Turn Locks",
                "Deadbolt Won't Extend or Retract",
                "Key Turns But Lock Doesn't Engage",
                "Loose or Rattling Lock Hardware",
                "Lock Cylinder Spins Freely",
                "Misaligned Lock & Strike Plate",
                "Broken Key Stuck Inside Lock",
                "Break-In Damage Repair",
                "Worn-Out Lock Mechanism",
                "Sliding Door Lock Repair",
              ].map((item) => (
                <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-gray-700">
                  <span class="w-6 h-6 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3 h-3 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3">
                      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                  {item}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
              <a
                href="tel:3027350050"
                class="w-full inline-flex justify-center items-center rounded-full bg-[#A61E22] px-6 py-3 text-white font-bold hover:bg-[#8C181B] transition"
              >
                Call (302) 735-0050 Now
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Common Lock Repairs</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">
          Lock Repair Services We Provide in Delaware
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Here's a detailed look at the most common lock problems we diagnose and repair for homeowners and businesses throughout Delaware. Don't see your issue listed? Just call — if it involves a lock, we can help.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8">

        <!-- Stiff / Hard to Turn -->
        <div id="stiff-lock" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.325 4.317c.426-1.756 2.924-1.756 3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 002.573 1.066c1.543-.94 3.31.826 2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 001.065 2.572c1.756.426 1.756 2.924 0 3.35a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.066 2.573c.94 1.543-.826 3.31-2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.572 1.065c-.426 1.756-2.924 1.756-3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.573-1.066c-1.543.94-3.31-.826-2.37-2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.065-2.572c-1.756-.426-1.756-2.924 0-3.35a1.724 1.724 0 001.066-2.573c-.94-1.543.826-3.31 2.37-2.37.996.608 2.296.07 2.572-1.065z" />
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Stiff or Hard-to-Turn Lock Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A key that's gradually getting harder to turn is one of the most common lock complaints we hear — and one of the most ignored. People tend to put up with a stiff lock for months, forcing the key a little harder each time, until the day it snaps off inside the cylinder or simply stops turning altogether. That's an easily preventable situation.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Stiff locks are usually caused by one of several things: dried-out or gunked-up internal lubrication, worn-down key pins that aren't moving freely, a warped or swollen door that's putting pressure on the lock body, or gradual internal wear from years of use. Our locksmiths diagnose the exact cause, clean and lubricate the mechanism, replace worn pins or springs if needed, and adjust the door alignment if that's contributing to the problem.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              In most cases a stiff lock can be brought back to smooth, reliable operation without replacement. If the internal damage is too extensive to repair cost-effectively, we'll tell you honestly and can handle a replacement on the same visit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deadbolt Won't Extend -->
        <div id="deadbolt-wont-extend" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 118 0m-4 8v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 002-2v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Deadbolt Won't Extend or Retract — Lock Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A deadbolt that won't fully extend or that gets stuck halfway is a serious security problem — a bolt that doesn't fully seat in the strike plate provides little to no forced entry resistance. This issue is more common than most people realize, particularly in older homes where doors have shifted, settled, or swollen seasonally.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              The most frequent cause is a misalignment between the deadbolt and the strike plate on the door frame. Over time, doors sag or shift, and what was once a perfect alignment drifts. The fix may be as straightforward as repositioning the strike plate, adjusting the door hinges, or planing a small amount of material from the door edge. In other cases the deadbolt mechanism itself has an internal fault — a broken cam, worn tailpiece, or damaged bolt assembly — which we can often repair or replace on-site.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              Don't rely on a deadbolt that isn't fully latching. Call us and we'll get it operating correctly so your door is actually secured when you lock it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Lock Cylinder Spins -->
        <div id="cylinder-spins" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Lock Cylinder Spinning Freely — Lock Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              If your key turns but nothing happens — the cylinder spins all the way around without engaging the bolt or latch — the connection between the cylinder and the lock mechanism has failed. This is typically caused by a broken or worn tailpiece (the small metal component that transfers rotation from the cylinder to the locking cam), a snapped retaining clip, or internal cam damage.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A freely spinning lock cylinder is an urgent repair — the lock is essentially non-functional and your door cannot be secured until it's fixed. In most cases this is a repairable problem involving replacing the internal tailpiece or cam assembly. If the lock body is severely worn or damaged, a full cylinder replacement is the better option and can often be done while retaining the same key if needed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              1st Capital Locksmith responds to urgent lock repairs throughout Delaware. If your lock is spinning and your door can't be secured, call (302) 735-0050 and we'll dispatch as quickly as possible.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Broken Key in Lock -->
        <div id="broken-key" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 7a2 2 0 012 2m4 0a6 6 0 01-7.743 5.743L11 17H9v2H7v2H4a1 1 0 01-1-1v-2.586a1 1 0 01.293-.707l5.964-5.964A6 6 0 1121 9z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Broken Key in Lock Extraction & Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              A key that snaps off inside a lock is one of those situations that almost always happens at the worst possible time. Attempting to extract it yourself with tweezers, a paperclip, or any improvised tool almost always makes the problem worse — pushing the key fragment deeper into the cylinder or damaging the internal pins in the process.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Our locksmiths use professional <a href="/services/broken-key-extraction" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">broken key extraction tools</a> to remove key fragments from lock cylinders cleanly without damaging the internal mechanism. In many cases the lock can be preserved and a new key cut once the broken piece is removed. After extraction we assess the condition of the lock — if the cylinder sustained damage during the break, we can repair or replace it on the same visit.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We also address the underlying cause. Keys don't usually break in good locks without reason — a worn key, a stiff lock, or a binding cylinder all increase the risk of breakage. We'll let you know if the lock itself needs attention to prevent a repeat.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Break-In Damage -->
        <div id="break-in-damage" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Break-In Damage Lock Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              If your property has been targeted in a break-in attempt — whether successful or not — your locks need professional assessment immediately. Attempted forced entry, picking, drilling, and bumping can all leave damage that isn't always visible from the outside but compromises the lock's internal security mechanisms. A lock that's been tampered with may appear to function normally while providing significantly reduced protection.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              1st Capital Locksmith assesses break-in damage to locks and door frames throughout Delaware. We examine the lock cylinder for signs of drilling or picking damage, check the bolt and latch mechanism for bending or distortion, and assess the door frame and strike plate for damage from kicking or prying. In most cases we recommend replacing a lock that's been compromised rather than repairing it — your security is the priority, not saving hardware that's been attacked.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              We carry replacement hardware and can upgrade your locks to stronger, higher-security options on the same visit. If you've experienced a break-in or a break-in attempt, call us right away — we'll get your property secured as quickly as possible.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Misaligned Lock -->
        <div id="misaligned-lock" class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm grid md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-6">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22] rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-white" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h8m-8 6h16" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-3">Misaligned Lock & Strike Plate Repair in Delaware</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Doors expand and contract seasonally, hinges loosen over time, and homes naturally settle on their foundations over the years. All of this gradually shifts the relationship between a lock bolt and the strike plate it needs to seat in. The result is a lock that catches, scrapes, sticks, or requires the door to be lifted or pushed just right in order to latch.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Misalignment is a very common lock complaint in Delaware homes, particularly in older properties and in the humid summer months when wooden doors swell. The fix usually involves adjusting or repositioning the strike plate, tightening or shimming the door hinges, or in some cases trimming the door edge. This is often a quick repair that restores smooth lock operation without needing to replace any hardware.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              If you're fighting with your door every time you try to lock it, don't keep forcing it. That kind of stress on the lock mechanism accelerates wear significantly. Call us and we'll get the alignment corrected properly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Commercial Lock Repair -->
